%description:

A deviation of the TR 38.901 UMa environment height from the specification
at one distance, recorded rather than fixed (model deviation 26). In TR
38.901 v16.1.0 Table 7.4.1-1 NOTE 1, g(d2D) = 0 for d2D <= 18 m, so at
d2D = 18 m C(d2D, hUT) = 0 and h_E is 1 m with certainty.
Tr38901PathLossModel::drawEnvironmentHeight() takes g = 0 only for
d2D < 18 m: at exactly 18 m it draws, and at hUT = 22.5 m about 5 links in
1000 get an h_E other than 1 m.

When fixed, drop the %expected-failure line and fold the checks into
PathLossEnvironmentHeight.

%expected-failure: the TR 38.901 h_E draw takes g(d2D) > 0 at d2D = 18 m

%includes:
#include "PathLossTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/stack/phy/channelmodel/Tr38901PathLossModel.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%activity:
CaseRecorder probe(this, 1e-6);
ScenarioParams p;
p.scenario = URBAN_MACROCELL;
p.hNodeB = 25;
p.hUe = 22.5;
p.carrierFrequencyGHz = 0.8;
Tr38901PathLossModel m;
p.apply(m, this);

long before = getRNG(0)->getNumbersDrawn();
int notOne = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 40000; i++)
    if (m.drawEnvironmentHeight(18) != 1)
        notOne++;
probe.expectValue("no number is drawn at d2D = 18 m, where C = 0", getRNG(0)->getNumbersDrawn() - before, 0);
probe.expectValue("...and h_E is 1 m", notOne, 0);

probe.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=2 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
